s it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image at the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5bed9d39a641447d13bd6b033b870dbee08c7a480dd54ce67069e74d3496d00</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Sonam Wangchuk says he is under house arrest in Ladakh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16a7196764c7a193385c1411110aa152a8debdd3ea89afe79aed7d42240954f0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T07:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-sonam-wangchuk-says-he-is-under-house-arrest-in-ladakh/live-79936475--47fb6447cba6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-sonam-wangchuk-says-he-is-under-house-arrest-in-ladakh/live-79936475?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Wangchuk is among activists in Ladakh who have raised concerns about upcoming regional elections, which they say are designed to diminish voter participation as they will be held in the harsh winter period. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US disrupts North Korea's $400 million crypto scam, FBI says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94bc96dd21cc1375e64bec1c2c1f758b449731305d541529d06ee0ce740ce2aa</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T04:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-disrupts-north-korea-s-400-million-crypto-scam-fbi-says/a-79935957--ed83d7896a38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-disrupts-north-korea-s-400-million-crypto-scam-fbi-says/a-79935957?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has seized servers linked to a North Korean scam that used fake video meetings and deepfakes to steal more than $400 million in crypto, and has moved to seize $1.2 billion that was taken from Binance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:838d0256d26b85dab86f4f07dfd2e1f2169da0120539fcd15cc74e9b2413b381</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law, but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89cacca9b340244bac27a114b3ab5b8734187b6eaa1891bc6dfae64d2e088aee</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi Jinping renews calls for 'reunification' with Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8c6edddacfcbda402c1e99df4d50fae88a32ab3d2be9f61619204234503655e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738--c3c1f561b896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping said that reunification was inevitable, but stopped short of mentioning military force. Taiwan though swiftly rejected Beijing's demands as tensions continue over the island's future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news : Modi government approves $340 million museum in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5f7e04294c3ce548bcddf7ef877c342488b01f77a2c2e174b4fccbf3dfda45e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477--8b8209e9e65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The government says that the 'Yuge Yugeen Bharat Museum' will have the world's "largest" museum dispaly area."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a8976e7225d3cca5c2d1db4ad1b2e63dba1698c9759cf1b99b3ab8bd6e1184c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a282a6c876382ac014fc4bb5de449ee3b62b5d644c064c7a484fe75f4bd809</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Japan watches for signs of change in Trump's foreign policy priorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54c364d4d8b8341a3a462e678b0ab6e79691d0d9d7318364bd960445c0a788ae</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398--c0dcb3ef3493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-watches-for-signs-of-change-in-trump-s-foreign-policy-priorities/a-79909398?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tokyo fears the drubbing US President Donald Trump suffered in last week's midterm election may push him to pursue a diplomatic quick win at the expense of Washington's allies in the Indo-Pacific.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's demonetization: 10 years on, economic benefits still disputed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dce68e99ebf9ea713ab693a8b88ea43d2a1b4e67651b0a14c66447fc41b5226</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331--2fc450e61f09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-demonetization-10-years-on-economic-benefits-still-disputed/a-79903331?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the 2016 currency ban, its impact on India's economy and the fight against black money remains contested.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13585655ca57fd0a73bc41af6a3cb21b46e7bd0376c12a288b6df7fbb5a73b2c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02cc59e70ebebd98bbea286f5220e6bfcd25278e40bf5bf3d48cc22e763eda</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
